# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and in every working
# tree. Without this, Git for Windows (`core.autocrlf=true` by default, including
# on GitHub-hosted `windows-*` runners) checks out CRLF and `cargo fmt --check`
# fails against `newline_style = "Unix"` in `rustfmt.toml`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF to remain executable by cmd.exe.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never normalize or diff binary content. Disposable disk fixtures are generated
# and git-ignored (SAFE-001, Section 11.3); these rules are a defense in depth in
# case one is ever added deliberately under a reviewed exception.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.img binary
*.raw binary
*.vhd binary
*.vhdx binary
*.qcow2 binary

# Generated lockfiles are reviewed but collapsed in pull-request diffs.
Cargo.lock linguist-generated=true
